from the Lord.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AE","section":"687","subsection":"6"},"text":"Counsel (), of which walking is predicated, has regard to thought.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AE","section":"696","subsection":"17"},"text":"His Divine wisdom and Divine power are signified by the spirit of wisdom and intelligence, and by the spirit of counsel and might ().","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AE","section":"721","subsection":"12"},"text":"Counsellor () = the understanding of the truth of the Word.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AE","section":"1100","subsection":"19"},"text":"A man of counsel () = a man who is intelligent from the truths which are from the good of love.","comment":null,"footnote":null}],"slug":"counsel","url":"/meta/potts/counsel/"}